  "title": "enterprises: const-ify the table and use array_length.",
  "description": "Using array_length eliminates the need to separately store the maximum index in\nthe list, allowing us to replace the \"struct\" with a simple array of strings.\n\nconst-ing the table moves 495 kBytes of data from a read-write section to a\nread-only section.\n\nFix a minor typo in a script comment (coma => comma).\n\nepan/enterprises.c was firstly regenerated with the 2024-05-23 enterprise list\n(the first commit), and was then regenerated with the same list and the updated\nscript in the second commit so that the effect of the script update would be\nisolated from the update of the underlying enterprise list.\n\nYou might need to choose \"Hide whitespace changes\" in the gitlab diff viewer\nbefore the changes to `epan/enterprises.c` will be shown.",
