      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1920711085,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "LGTM, I assume array_length() is done compile-time, so global_enterprises_lookup() will be quick?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-05-24T13:04:35.832Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-05-25T09:11:46.621Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 304022901,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2024-05-25T09:11:46.621Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 15735,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1921598808,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "That's correct.  `array_length(arr)` is just a macro which expands to `sizeof arr / sizeof arr[0]`, and that's a compile-time constant equal to the number of elements in the array, so the generated code will contain direct comparisons against that immediate value representing the array length.  Nice and fast.\n\nFor example:\n```\n$ objdump -drlS ../wireshark-ninja/epan/CMakeFiles/epan.dir/enterprises.c.o \n\n../wireshark-ninja/epan/CMakeFiles/epan.dir/enterprises.c.o:     file format elf64-x86-64\n\n\nDisassembly of section .text:\n\n0000000000000000 <global_enterprises_lookup>:\nglobal_enterprises_lookup():\n/home/dariusd/wireshark/wireshark/epan/enterprises.c:61966\n    \"Genew Technologies Co., Ltd.\",                                                       // 61939\n    \"Excard Research GmbH\"                                                                // 61940\n};\n\nconst char* global_enterprises_lookup(uint32_t value)\n{\n   0:\t55                   \tpush   %rbp\n   1:\t48 89 e5             \tmov    %rsp,%rbp\n   4:\t89 7d fc             \tmov    %edi,-0x4(%rbp)\n/home/dariusd/wireshark/wireshark/epan/enterprises.c:61967\n    if (value >= array_length(table)) {\n   7:\t81 7d fc f4 f1 00 00 \tcmpl   $0xf1f4,-0x4(%rbp)\n   e:\t76 07                \tjbe    17 <global_enterprises_lookup+0x17>\n/home/dariusd/wireshark/wireshark/epan/enterprises.c:61968\n        return NULL;\n  10:\tb8 00 00 00 00       \tmov    $0x0,%eax\n  15:\teb 16                \tjmp    2d <global_enterprises_lookup+0x2d>\n[... etc ...]\n```\n\nThe `0xf1f4` in the comparison instruction at offset 7 is decimal 61940, which is the index of the last element in the array, so the \"jump if below or equal\" is correctly evaluating whether `value` is within the array bounds, using the array length value determined at compile time.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7889756,
            "username": "dariusd0",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "dariusd0",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f0f4a609abaf984c9cfe277f1321b8db104aea7290fcbb7fb0c5749a00d32e39?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/dariusd0"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-05-24T21:27:44.298Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-05-25T09:11:46.621Z",
