      "title": "enterprises: const-ify the table and use array_length.",
      "message": "enterprises: const-ify the table and use array_length.\n\nUsing array_length eliminates the need to separately store the maximum index in\nthe list, allowing us to replace the \"struct\" with a simple array of strings.\n\nconst-ing the table moves 495 kBytes of data from a read-write section to a\nread-only section.\n\nFix a minor typo in a script comment (coma => comma).\n\nepan/enterprises.c was regenerated with the 2024-05-23 enterprise list, so the\nlist content is unchanged from the prior manual update.\n",
      "author_name": "Darius Davis",
      "author_email": "darius-wireshark@free-range.com.au",
      "authored_date": "2024-05-24T20:16:15.000+10:00",
      "committer_name": "Martin Mathieson",
